No, creating the exception files is NOT enough.
You MUST change your existing Service and Controller files.
Here is why:
Your GlobalExceptionHandler is like a catcher's mitt. It is waiting to catch specific errors.
Your Service code is the pitcher. Right now, your service code is either:
 * Holding the ball: Swallowing exceptions with try { ... } catch (Exception e) { log.error(...) } (The handler never sees it).
 * Throwing a different ball: Throwing generic RuntimeException or IOException (The handler catches it as a generic "Internal Server Error" instead of the specific error you defined).
To make this work, you must modify your code to throw the specific exceptions you just created.
Here are the 4 exact locations you must change to activate your new strategy.
