4. Modify AsyncConfig.java
You MUST implement AsyncConfigurer here.
If an exception occurs in a @Async method (like executeAsyncBatchCreation), it happens in a separate thread. The Controller never sees it, and the GlobalExceptionHandler never sees it. It just disappears into the logs.
Change To:
@Configuration
@EnableAsync
@Slf4j
public class AsyncConfig implements AsyncConfigurer { // 1. Implement this interface

    // ... your existing bean definition for bulkExecutor ...

    // 2. Add this method to catch Async failures
    @Override
    public AsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler getAsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler() {
        return (Throwable ex, Method method, Object... params) -> {
            log.error("CRITICAL ASYNC FAILURE in method: {}", method.getName(), ex);
            // Ideally, you would update the Batch Status to 'ERROR' in the DB here
            // so the user knows it failed.
        };
    }
}

Summary of Necessary Changes
 * Service Layer: Change throw new RuntimeException() to throw new [YourCustomException]().
 * Controller Layer: Delete try-catch blocks and let exceptions float up.
 * Config Layer: Add AsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler so background threads don't fail silently.
